[9.941605, "o", " terminal background as possible, or have a         \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[15;1H\u001b[2K    \u001b[38;2;1;2;38mspecified \u001b[39m\u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;1;2;38mpreferred\u001b[39m\u001b[23m\u001b[38;2;1;2;38m\u001b[38;2;1;2;38m contrast?\u001b[39m                                                                   \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[16;1H\u001b[2K                                                                                                    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[17;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[38;2;1;2;38mThen the generator can search lightness along each hue/saturation curve for the color that         \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[18;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[38;2;1;2;38msatisfies the required ratios, checking the final hex with Color.js. Where one token appears on    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[19;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[38;2;1;2;38mseveral surfaces, it must satisfy all of them. Preferred ratios can guide the choice, but some may \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[20;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[38;2;1;2;38mbe mutually impossible; those should be reported rather than silently treated as achieved.\u001b[39m         \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[21;1H\u001b[2K                                                                                    "]
